      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1904, Ahn Chang Ho established the first American Koreatown, called Pachappa Camp, in Riverside.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inland_Empire",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The hydroelectric‑powered irrigation colonies of Etiwanda and Upland were launched by the Chaffey Brothers, while Matthew Gage built the Gage Canal in Riverside during the 1880s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
